---
import { settings } from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PrivacyRequestForm from '../components/PrivacyRequestForm.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description={`How ${settings.businessName} handles website inquiries and privacy requests. This draft requires owner review before public launch.`}
>
  <section class="vss-page-hero vss-container privacy-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">
      <span class="eyebrow-dot"></span>PRIVACY NOTICE · OWNER APPROVAL REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH
    </p>
    <h1>Your information<br />deserves <em>care.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      This notice describes the information collected through this website, why it is used, and how
      to submit a privacy request.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="privacy-content vss-container">
    <aside class="privacy-index">
      <span>ON THIS PAGE</span><a href="#controller">Who is responsible</a><a href="#collected"
        >What we collect</a
      ><a href="#use">How we use it</a><a href="#retention">Retention</a><a href="#requests"
        >Your requests</a>
    </aside>
    <div class="privacy-copy">
      <div class="draft-callout">
        <strong>Owner review required:</strong> Before accepting real inquiries, confirm the legal business
        identity, privacy contact, service providers, approved retention period, and rules that apply
        in the regions served. This draft is not legal advice or a substitute for an owner-approved notice.
      </div>
      <section id="controller">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / RESPONSIBILITY</p><h2>Who is responsible?</h2><p>
          The business operating as <strong data-site-content="businessName">{site.name}</strong> is
          responsible for the information submitted through this website. Submit a privacy request using
          the form below or through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
        </p><p
          class="privacy-email-note"
          data-site-email-group="privacy"
          hidden={!site.privacyEmail}
        >
          You may also email the privacy contact at <a
            data-site-email="privacy"
            href={site.privacyEmail ? 'mailto:' + site.privacyEmail : undefined}
            hidden={!site.privacyEmail}>{site.privacyEmail}</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="collected">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / INFORMATION</p><h2>What may we collect?</h2><p>
          If you submit an inquiry, we collect your name, email address, optional business and phone
          details, the service and optional package you select, and your message. If you send a privacy request, we
          collect your name, email, request type, and details needed to respond.
        </p><p>
          Please do not include passwords, payment details, or sensitive personal information in a
          message.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="use">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / PURPOSE</p><h2>How is it used?</h2><p>
          Inquiry details are used to understand and respond to your request, manage the inquiry,
          and record follow-up. Privacy request details are used to verify, process, and document
          the request. The website uses a hidden honeypot field and request limits to reduce
          automated submissions.
        </p><p>
          This form is not a marketing signup. Inquiry contacts are not added to a mailing list
          through this form.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / SERVICE PROVIDERS</p><h2>Where is it processed?</h2><p>
          The current implementation uses Netlify to serve the website and API functions, Supabase
          to store inquiry and staff records and manage staff sign-in, and Resend for owner email
          notices if enabled. The business owner must confirm the active providers, account
          settings, and processing locations before launch.
        </p>
        {import.meta.env.PUBLIC_HCAPTCHA_SITE_KEY && <p>
          We use hCaptcha to verify form submissions and help prevent automated abuse.
          See <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy">hCaptcha's privacy policy</a>
          for information about its verification service.
        </p>}
      </section>
      <section id="retention">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 / RETENTION</p><h2>How long is it kept?</h2><p>
          The implementation is configured to anonymize unconverted inquiries after 12 months
          without activity. Converted client records follow the business’s separate contractual and
          legal retention needs. The owner must approve these periods before launch.
        </p><p>
          Encrypted backups have a separate expiry schedule. If a backup is restored, completed
          deletion and correction requests must be reapplied before the system returns to service.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="requests">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 / YOUR REQUESTS</p><h2>Ask about your information.</h2><p>
          You can request access, correction, export, or deletion using the form below. The business
          verifies identity before acting. Some business records may need to be retained where a
          legal or contractual requirement applies; if so, the business should explain that
          decision.
        </p>
      </section>
      <div class="privacy-request-area"><PrivacyRequestForm /></div>
      <p class="privacy-date">
        Draft notice version <span data-site-content="privacyNoticeVersion"
          >{site.noticeVersion}</span
        >. Replace with the owner-approved effective date before public launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
